<title>BELGIUM: CLABECQ RECEIVERS TO TRY SAVING FIRM.</title>
<headline>CLABECQ RECEIVERS TO TRY SAVING FIRM.</headline>
<dateline>CHARLEROI, Belgium 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The four official receivers appointed on Friday to run bankrupt steelmaker Forges de Clabecq said on Monday they aimed to try keeping the firm running and to continue supplying customers.</p>
<p>They said in a statement after an initial meeting with workers' representatives that they would try to reengage all 1,400 sacked employees -- albeit only on limited term contracts.</p>
<p>The statement stressed that simply because the firm had been declared bankrupt it did not automatically follow that it had ceased to exist or that there was no hope of salvation.</p>
<p>There was no immediate reaction from the unions.</p>
